From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:12:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SfxrInstance::getAudio: give no audio once the sound has
 ended

Called again after the sound's end, as the generic seek does while it
discards, getAudio went on past the envelope's last stage and read
env_length[3], past the array. An ended sound now returns 0 frames.
---
 src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp b/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp
index ca948ff..e3455de 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 	unsigned int SfxrInstance::getAudio(float *aBuffer, unsigned int aSamplesToRead, unsigned int /*aBufferSize*/)
 	{
+		// Called again after the end (the generic seek does), the envelope
+		// read past env_length: an ended sound gives nothing more.
+		if (!playing_sample)
+			return 0;
 		float *buffer = aBuffer;
 		unsigned int i;
 		for (i = 0; i < aSamplesToRead; i++)
